# `DESC` in caps is DS0105, and the key still sorts descending (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
from T | sort by a DESC
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..24
  PIPELINE@0..23
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "T"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    SORT_OP@9..23
      IDENT@9..13 "sort"
      WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
      IDENT@14..16 "by"
      WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
      SORT_KEY@17..23
        NAME_REF@17..18
          IDENT@17..18 "a"
        WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
        IDENT@19..23 "DESC"
  WHITESPACE@23..24 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `DESC` is not a sort direction
  --> query:1:20
  |
1 | from T | sort by a DESC
  |                    ^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: keywords are lowercase: write `desc`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from T | sort by a desc
which parses without errors
